## Conventions

- All tables use `tenant_id` (text) for row-level isolation — never query without it
- Timestamps: `created_at` (with timezone, defaultNow), `updated_at` (with timezone, defaultNow)
- PKs: `serial` (integer auto-increment) for most tables; `text` for `tenants.id` and `model_policies.tenant_id`
- JSONB: `hyperparams`, `metadata`, `level_scores` — always use `JSON.stringify()` when inserting
- Status enums are text columns (not PostgreSQL enums) for flexibility

## Tenant Auto-Provision

When a new user first hits `POST /forge/workspaces` or `POST /onboarding/provision`:

```sql
INSERT INTO tenants (id, name, user_id, plan)
VALUES ($tenantId, 'My Workspace', $userId, 'free')
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING
```

`tenantId` is derived from `userId`: `tenant-${userId.replace(/[^a-z0-9]/gi, '-').toLowerCase().slice(0, 32)}`

## Credential Security

Connector credentials encrypted with AES-256-GCM:
- Key material: PBKDF2-derived from `SESSION_SECRET` (100k iterations)
- Stored: `encrypted_credential` + `iv` in `tenant_connectors`
- Raw credentials NEVER returned in any API response
- Implementation: `lib/crypto-utils/src/index.ts`

## Full-Text Search (Knowledge Graphs)

Graph chunks use PostgreSQL `tsvector` with GIN index:
```sql
SELECT * FROM graph_chunks
ORDER BY ts_rank(tsv, plainto_tsquery($query)) DESC
```

Chunks are ~512 characters with 50-character overlap.
